>
  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>Political science career options in India go far past "become an IAS officer or teach
    it later."</strong> The real map includes policy research, corporate government affairs, law,
    journalism, diplomacy, NGOs, academia, and political consulting — each with a genuinely
    different pay ceiling, timeline, and risk. The track you pick matters less than whether you
    build a real, high-income skill portfolio inside it — research depth, writing, negotiation, and
    now AI-assisted analysis — because that combination decides your income ceiling and how early
    you reach financial freedom, not the job title on your degree.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Political science leads to at least 9 real tracks, not two. UPSC and State PSC are only one of them, and honestly not the one with the strongest growth curve.</li>
      <li>The strongest long-term ceiling usually sits in political and policy consulting or an independent research platform you own, followed by corporate government affairs — both scale in ways a fixed government pay scale or an NGO grant cycle cannot.</li>
      <li>Civil services and academia both hide a second, separate competition after the one you already know about. Clearing the entry filter does not end the climb — it starts a new one.</li>
      <li><strong>Building a genuine high-income skill portfolio — research depth, writing, data literacy, and negotiation — is what turns any of these nine tracks into earlier financial freedom. The degree label alone does not.</strong></li>
      <li>Run the track you are leaning toward through The 4-Checkpoint Protocol before you commit years of exam prep, a PhD, or an unpaid internship season to it.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p>
    If you are still deciding whether a humanities path fits you at all before narrowing this far,
    read <a href="/blog/career-options/">the Career Options category</a> for the wider set of guides
    on arts and humanities-adjacent paths.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you are close to a real decision here — starting UPSC prep, applying to law school, or
    picking between a PhD and a job — a session inside
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career guidance</a>
    can help you weigh this specific move against your own finances and runway, not a generic list.
  </p>

  <nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Article sections">
    <p class="jump-nav__label">Jump to section</p>
    <ul class="jump-nav__list">
      {jumpLinks.map((item) => (
        <li><a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.label}</a></li>
      ))}
    </ul>
